module wiwd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The Western District of Wisconsin's own periods, computed under FRCP
// 6(a), which governs a period stated in a local rule. The five Local
// Rules state one period: the thirty days after the defendants' appearance
// within which litigants consider alternative dispute resolution (L.R. 3,
// the court's LR 16.6 CJ). The others state none: admission of lawyers and
// reciprocal discipline (L.R. 1), the magistrate judges' designation (L.R.
// 2), contacting jurors (L.R. 4) and electronic filing (L.R. 5). The
// admission fee is "the prescribed fee" (L.R. 1(B), (C)) and is not stated
// in the vendored text, so it stays out. The earlier W.D. Wis. outline's
// FRCP flow and its Supreme Court decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex,
// Anderson v. Liberty Lobby) are FRCP authority and belong to lit/frcp and
// lit/frap; its Seventh Circuit decisions (Cracco v. Vitran Express, Inc.;
// Swanson v. Citibank, N.A.) are removed: no reporter text is vendored.
// Seventh Circuit rules and operating procedures are not vendored either.
/// The defendants appear in a civil case that L.R. 3(D) does not exempt
/// (L.R. 3(A)).
event DefendantsAppeared()

/// L.R. 3(A): litigants are to consider the use of alternative dispute
/// resolution within thirty days of the defendants' appearance. Cases in
/// which the plaintiff proceeds pro se, collection and United States
/// mortgage foreclosure actions, Social Security appeals, and bankruptcy
/// matters other than adversary proceedings are exempt (L.R. 3(D)).
deadline adr-consideration-period: 30.days after DefendantsAppeared() counted_by frcp6 cite "W.D. Wis. L.R. 3"

test "adr consideration period: 30 days after the defendants appear" cite "W.D. Wis. L.R. 3"
{
  given DefendantsAppeared() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(adr-consideration-period) == 2026-12-02
}
